# 🏨 Hotel Management System — MERN Stack with End-to-End DevOps Pipeline

A full-featured **Hotel Management System** built on the **MERN stack** (MongoDB, Express, React, Node.js), engineered with a **production-grade DevOps pipeline** covering containerization, orchestration, infrastructure as code, security scanning, code quality gates, and CI/CD automation.

> This repository is not just an application — it's a demonstration of a complete DevOps workflow, from code commit to a running, scanned, and monitored container in Kubernetes.


## 🧱 Tech Stack

### Application
| Layer | Technology |
|---|---|
| Frontend | React.js, Redux/Context API, Axios, Bootstrap/Tailwind |
| Backend | Node.js, Express.js, REST API |
| Database | MongoDB (Mongoose ORM) |
| Auth | JWT-based Authentication |

### DevOps & Infrastructure
| Category | Tool |
|---|---|
| Version Control | Git & GitHub |
| Containerization | Docker, Docker Compose |
| Orchestration | Kubernetes (K8s) |
| Infrastructure as Code | Terraform |
| CI/CD | Jenkins (Declarative Pipeline) |
| Code Quality | SonarQube |
| Security Scanning | Trivy (Image & Filesystem scan) |
| Container Registry | DockerHub  |
| Cloud Provider | `[AWS ` |
| Monitoring  | `[Prometheus + Grafana]` |

---

## 🏗️ Architecture Overview

```
Developer Push (GitHub)
        │
        ▼
   Jenkins Pipeline Triggered (Webhook)
        │
   ┌────┴─────────────────────────────────┐
   │  1. Checkout Code                    │
   │  2. SonarQube Static Code Analysis   │
   │  3. Build Docker Images (FE + BE)    │
   │  4. Trivy Image Vulnerability Scan   │
   │  5. Push Image to Registry           │
   │  6. Terraform Provision/Update Infra │
   │  7. Deploy to Kubernetes (kubectl)   |
   |     via kubeconfig                   │
   │  8. Post-deploy health check         │
   └──────────────────────────────────────┘
        │
        ▼
   Kubernetes Cluster (EKS)
   ├── Frontend Deployment + Service
   ├── Backend Deployment + Service
   ├── MongoDB StatefulSet + PVC
   └── Ingress Controller (NGINX)
```


